# [[.ID]]

A Heimdall suite written by `bifrost-bench suite init -template [[.Template]]`,
with one complete sample task (`tasks/[[.Sample]]`). The user guide is
`docs/external-apis.md` in the bench repository.

[[.About]]

## What to edit

1. `tasks/<task>/task.yaml`, `external:`: the API's `base_url`, the
   allowlist (`allow`: methods and path prefixes the agent may call; anything
   else is refused), static `headers`, and `auth_env`, the name of the host
   environment variable holding the credential. The proxy adds it; the agent
   never sees it, and it is redacted from the ledger and the cassette.
2. `tasks/<task>/cassettes/<id>.cassette.jsonl`: the recorded calls a
   replay run is answered from, one JSON object per line. Record a real one
   with an experiment that sets `external: record`, then copy
   `runs/<exp>/<run>/external/<id>.cassette.jsonl` here (see the guide).
3. `tasks/<task>/repo/`: what the agent starts with (here the API's docs).
4. `tasks/<task>/instruction.md`: the request, as a user would write it.
5. `tasks/<task>/verifier/tests/verify.py`: what the agent's output must hold.
6. `tasks/<task>/solution/reference.sh`: the calls a correct agent makes,
   through the proxy. Admission runs it in the agent's place, in replay
   mode, and the verifier must pass it.

`controls/` holds what admission requires to fail: the empty control, a
mutant (a plausible wrong result) and an exploit that tries to leave the
allowlist (another path, another host through the proxy) and fakes a result.

## Layout

```
suite.yaml                               track tool_use, verifier_command with a reward
probes/model-outage.yaml                 gateway fault
probes/fx-error-first.yaml               tool fault on the external API's first call
tasks/[[.Sample]]/task.yaml              external: the fx API, allowlist, cassette
tasks/[[.Sample]]/cassettes/             recorded API calls (replay mode)
tasks/[[.Sample]]/repo/API.md            the API docs the agent reads
tasks/[[.Sample]]/verifier/tests/        hidden verifier
tasks/[[.Sample]]/solution/reference.sh  reference control
tasks/[[.Sample]]/controls/              empty, mutant and exploit controls
```

## Check it

```
bifrost-bench suite lint [[.ID]]
bifrost-bench suite lock [[.ID]]
bifrost-bench suite admit [[.ID]]
```

Admission and every run that does not opt in use replay mode: no call
leaves the bench. Live mode costs repeatability: the API may answer
differently tomorrow, so reports and the leaderboard label or exclude it.

## Held-out tasks and canaries

Add `split: held_out` to a task's `task.yaml` to keep it out of `tasks: all`,
out of the public leaderboard and out of what the UI and API serve. To detect
later whether this suite leaked into a model's training data, give it a
contamination canary:

    bifrost-bench suite canary [[.ID]]          # sets canary: <guid> in suite.yaml
    bifrost-bench suite canary -stamp [[.ID]]   # also writes it into every instruction file
    bifrost-bench suite canary-check -text model-output.txt

Stamping changes instruction hashes, so run `suite lock` and `suite admit`
again afterwards; stamp before the first published results, not after. A
canary only catches verbatim copies of stamped text. The bench guide
`docs/held-out-and-canaries.md` has the details.
